2 CONT https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/Digitised/Article/singfreepressb18920229-1.2.12?ST=1&AT=advanced&K=tan%20kim%20ching&KA=tan%20kim%20ching&DF=&DT=16%2F03%2F1900&Display=0&NPT=&L=&CTA=&QT=tan,kim,ching&oref=article
2 CONT
2 CONT Vice Consul of Siam holding the title "Khoon Rasada Borirax"
2 CONT
2 CONT Soon Toh, the eldest son of Tan Kim Cheng. Soon Toh married Wuing Yi Ho, the daughter of Wuing Boon Whatt who according to Song Ong Siang, was the first Chinese in Singapore to practise law. Like his father, Soon Toh was an active
2 CONC  leader of the Chinese community. He was also listed in the Singapore General Directory in 1890 as the Vice Consul of Siam holding the title "Khoon Rasada Borirax". Many thanks to Rosalind Leong nee Wee Choo Neo for showing me thi
2 CONC s very rare photo which has her mom's (Molly Tan Leng Neo) handwriting -- setting out details of the Tan lineage -- on the back of the photo.
2 CONT
