1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tan Jiak Kim (陈若锦) (b. 29 April 1859, Singapore–d. 22 October 1917, Singapore) was a prominent Straits-born Chinese (Peranakan) merchant and political activist in the early 19th century. He was an outstanding commu
2 CONC nity leader who contributed significantly to the Straits Settlements community and donated generously to the less fortunate. Tan co-founded the Straits Chinese British Association (SCBA) to facilitate the interests of the Straits-
2 CONC born Chinese and to unite the elite in a pledge of undivided loyalty to the British. He was also a successful businessman in the banking and insurance industries.
2 CONT
