1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Funeral August 1934: https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/maltribune19340829-1.2.180
2 CONT
2 CONT From his son Tan Teng Ann's tombstone write-up:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Tan Tiam Hock of Malacca celebrated his 74th birthday on 29 July 1927. Mr. Tan Tiam Hock is the father of 
2 CONT Mr. Tan Teng Ann, of Boustead and Co. Singapore
2 CONT Mr. Tan Gim Ann, an old School boy who is taking the B.A course in Hong Kong 
2 CONT Mr. Tan Soon Ann and Tan Tam Kim who are now in Malacca.
2 CONT Mr. Tan Tiam Hock was, like the late. Mr. Tan Chay Yan and others who whom he was associated, a pioneer rubber planter of Malacca. He was a part owner of Bukit Asahan Estate (now owned by the Malacca Rubber Plantations, Ltd. The n
2 CONC ewspapers went to mention that of the original owners of this estste, the only survivors are Mr. Tan Tiam Hock and Dr. Lim Boon Keng. 
