1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Straits Times / Obituary, Illustration
2 CONT Lock icon Untitled
2 CONT 30 September 2007 - 2nd Anniversary In Loving Memory Of SALLY CHEANG LYE NEO (Wife of the Late Orchard Poh Whatt Chye) Departed 30 September 2005 Always remembered by family and loved ones
2 CONT 29 words 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mdm Cheang Lye Neo (Sally), was the fifth daughter of Mr. & Mrs. Cheang Seng Kay. She was married to Po Whatt Chye (Orchard) on Sunday, 16th June, 1940 (as recorded in a two-part Statutory Declaration). They had a wedding dinner a
2 CONC t the residence of her adoptive father-in-law, Mr. Po Kim Yong, at No. 161, Pasir Panjang Road (6 3/4 milestone), on the same day, as recorded in their wedding invitation dated 10 June 1940. The Pasir Panjang address does not corr
2 CONC espond with the present No. 161 Pasir Panjang Road as the housing numbers were renamed over the years. Miss Cheang Lye Neo had 11 biological children from her marriage to Po Whatt Chye.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her favourite colour was purple (amethyst) and she was a Protestant at the time of her death. Her niche is at Holy Family Church Columbarium, St. Anne's section.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Updated by Nicole Poh (grand-daughter) on 19 August 2022, with reference to the original copy of her statutory declaration, and wedding invitation with Po Whatt Chye.
