2 CONT "Luckily, the account of Li Qinghui 李清輝, himself a Baba of Malacca, has been preserved. Luckily, the account of Li Qinghui 李清輝, himself a Baba of Malacca, has been preserved (11). Along with his brother Cheng Yan清渊"
2 CONT
2 CONT (11) The Lat Po was founded in 1881 by See Ewe Lay 薛有禮, a fifth generation Baba from Malacca who was born in Singapore where his grandfather had settled down in 1828. The newspaper however was run by a newspaperman born in China w
2 CONC ho had previously worked in Hong Kong for the Chung Ngoi San Po 中外新報 (founded in 1860); cf. Chen Mong Hock, The Early Chinese Newspapers of Singapore 1881-1912, Singapore, University of Malaya Press, 1967, pp. 18, 24-25. The trave
2 CONC logue appeared in 1889 (issues n° 2162, 2d month, 12th day to n° 2180, 3rd month, 5th day).
