1 NAME Cheng Kiat /CHAN/
2 GIVN Cheng Kiat
2 SURN CHAN
2 _MARNM CHAN
1 NAME CHAN Cheng Kiat
1 NAME 清吉 //
2 GIVN 清吉
2 SURN 曾
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1867
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 NOV 1936
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Singapore
1 OCCU Cashier
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} CHAN Cheng Kiat's gravestone is located in Bukit Brown (Block 4 Division A). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family relationships for his second wife Mrs Chan Cheng Kiat nee Tan Geok Lin Neo: https://mymindisrojak.blogspot.com/2021/03/tan-teng-ann-bukit-brown.html
2 CONT
2 CONT His first child was daughter CHAN Geok Eng (~1889-91, died during Japanese Occupation)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please note, there is a different individual (or more than one!) by the same name of CHAN Cheng Kiat from Malacca around the same era:
2 CONT
2 CONT > born 1898, died 28 February 1985 (obituary: https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/straitstimes19850313-1.2.55.4)
2 CONT > is listed as among the key founders of Malacca Buddhist Association Seck Kia Eenh (www.ske.my) w/ corresponding newspaper articles
2 CONT
2 CONT > passed Junior Cambridge in 1917 (https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/singfreepresswk19170614-1.2.54)
2 CONT > Malacca Volunteer Corps Lance Corporal 1928, Sergeant 1934, Command Sergeant Major 1938 
2 CONT > is assistant treasurer for Malacca Chinese Football Club for many years
2 CONT > played tennis
2 CONT > won at rifle shooting
2 CONT
2 CONT > is honorary auditor for Malacca Mercantile Cooperative Thrift and Loan Society 1929
2 CONT > is Treasurer for the Pan-Malayan Council of Clerical Unions, 1948
2 CONT > is part of the Malacca Chinese Benevolent Association, 1955
2 CONT > is Treasurer to the Straits Chinese British Association, 1962
2 CONT
2 CONT > is charged with a chap ji kee gambling offence in Singapore in 1939 (https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/singfreepressb19400507-1.2.56)
2 CONT > is charged with a second lottery offence, 1940
2 CONT
2 CONT > is charged with a lottery offence 1967 (https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/straitstimes19670516-1.2.146). 
2 CONT
2 CONT > Is a clerk for Boustead and Co, and declares Bankruptcy 1929
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no telling which events belong to which or how many individuals, except in this case for the fact of being based in Singapore after 1890 and dying in 1936. 
2 CONT
2 CONT However in one case, a newspaper article in 1918/1919 reporting contributing activities in Malacca, at this "Malacca Day Fete" organized by millionaire E Kong Guan, he was married (3rd wife) to one of this Chan Cheng Kiat's nieces
2 CONC
2 CONT (https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/maltribune19190324-1.2.34). 
