1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Madam Lim Siak Neo's tomb is very accessible and can be seen from the main access road in and out of Bukit Brown and is also is an interesting tomb not because of its size and grandeur but its children have surname
2 CONC s, Wee and Sng. Did she marry a Wee (and after her first spouse passed away, remarried to a Sng ?) We can match the Sng children to her husband's tomb, Mr. Sng Kan Ngah in Hill 3 Section B, plot 641.
2 CONT
2 CONT Madam Lim Siak Neo passed away at the age of 75 on 8th January 1932 at her residence No 44 Hindoo Road. She is survived by 4 sons; Wee Teck Swee, Wee Teck Bock, Wee Teck Leong, Sng Teck Hoe, 4 daughters-in-law, 5 daughters, 5 son-
2 CONC in-laws;  Teh Ewe Lan (of Amoy, China), Ee Kee Seng, Chee Swee Kiat, Tan Joo Kian and Tan Soon Leong, 46 grandchildren;  eldest are; Teh Seng Kay (of Kampar), Wee Guan Ho, Wee Guan Hai, Wee Guan Keh, Peng Lim, 2 grandsons-in-law; 
2 CONC Tan Tiow Suan, Goh Hood Teh (of Bidor) and 2 grand daughters-in-law. 
2 CONT
