2 CONT
2 CONT Name: TAN Wi Yan Sex: M Birth: 1881 in Malacca 1 Death: 9 JAN 1935 in 27-3 Blair Road, Singapore 2 Burial: 1935 Bukit Brown, Singapore 3 Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Was born and educated in Malacca. Like TCY, he inherited numerous houses and parcels of land in Malacca and Singapore. First married Madam Chee who bore him a son, Hong Ghee. Followed Hoon Siang's footstep by studying in Engla
2 CONC nd. In later years, he migrated to Hong Kong. Second married Cheong Siow Ying from whom 4 sons were born. They were Chi Kong, Chee Wah, Chee Woh and Chee Lam. Became a successful merchant and miner. He was the executive partner of
2 CONC  the firm, Hup Liong Co, located at No. 4 Beach Road. His other company, Hap Liong Co., of which J C Robertson was a partner, was given extensive rights by the Sultan of Johore to mine tin in the Ulu Jemluang Valley. During the wa
2 CONC r, TWY together with his 2 business partners, Mr Sim Cheng Mia and Tan Kim Wah, donated a warplane to the British Government. The fighter plane was known as the "Wi Cheng Kim" or Malaya No. 4. Had a penchant for fine living. Was a
2 CONC mong the earliest in Singapore to own a Rolls Royce. The Silver Ghost bore the number S484. A copy of a photograph showing TWY and his Rolls Royce is kept in the National Heritage Board. TWY is buried in Bukit Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Lived at 285 River Valley Road, Singapore
2 CONT
