1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lee Keng Yam was well known as the head of the Opium Farms since 1885. Before this, he was in Messrs. Kim Seng and Co. based in Shanghai for 13 years before moving to Singapore in 1885. He holds the Dutch farms lic
2 CONC ense as well and 3 months before his death secured a 3 year license for the Hong Kong Opium Farm. He died in September 28, 1888 at his residence in Teluk Ayer Street at the age of 46 and buried in Malacca.
2 CONT
