1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mr Chua Guan Chui ( Chua Guan Chwee or also spelt as Chua Guan Swee ) from what little information i gathered was a property owner who bought property and rented them out. In a Strait Times article dated 1994, ther
2 CONC e was mentioned of two bungalows at No. 31 and 33 Scotts Road that in the 1920's belonged to the estate of Chua Guan Chui before it was eventually acquired by the Government in 1981.
2 CONT
2 CONT The home of Mr. Chua Guan Chui was called Darlington House, 75 Cairnhill Road. The family was evicted by the Japanese military administration from their house and they moved to No 152, Cairnhill Road.
