1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tan Hay Kwan's mainland Chinese roots may be traced back to his paternal ancestor Tan Cheng, a 7th-century governor of Chiang Chew in Fukien province during the early Tang dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a young man, Hay Kwan was one of several brothers who sailed from Fukien across the 'Southern Ocean' (南洋 or Nanyang) in search of a better life. He became a junk owner who plied his trade between Macassar in the Indonesian Cele
2 CONC bes (now Sulawesi) and Malacca, before finally settling in Malacca around 1770.
2 CONT
2 CONT Putting down his own roots in Malacca, Hay Kwan eventually died there and was buried alongside his wife Lee Chye Neo at Bukit Temporong.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Sources: C. Sanger, 'Malcolm MacDonald: Bringing an End to Empire', Liverpool: Liverpool University Press, 1996, p. 304; S. S. Tan, 'Goh Keng Swee: A Portrait', Singapore: Editions Didier Millet, 2007, p. 25; and Tan family recor
2 CONC ds, including 'A Biography of Mr. Tan Cheng Tiong'.)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Tan Hay Kwan  came from Province f Fujian, District of Nam Cheng Kwi (南靖縣), Village of Teck Hong (竹黃) Siah in Chiang Chew (泉州) prefecture in Fujian province to Malacca betweem 1771 to 1781
2 CONT --------------------
