2 CONT CHUA Whay Seng's death 1948
2 CONT https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/Digitised/Article/straitstimes19480218-1.2.35
2 CONT
2 CONT https://tombs.bukitbrown.org/2020/03/po-kim-soon.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Po Whatt Chye is the adoptive son of Tan Seng Neo (adoptive mother) and Po/Poh Kim Yong (adoptive father), the brother of his biological mother, Po/Poh Beng Neo (daughter of Po/Poh Jiat Pong) and her husband Chua Whay Seng. He was
2 CONC  born in Singapore Settlement in 1917. He attended Radin Mas school and Outram Afternoon School (15 January 1933 to 30 September 1934). He passed the Standard Six examination 1933 and thereafter sought employment. He was described
2 CONC  by his Principal as "Obedient, industrious. Should do well." 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Miss Cheang Lye Neo (Sally), the fifth daughter of Mr. & Mrs. Cheang Seng Kay on Sunday, 16th June, 1940 (as recorded in a two-part Statutory Declaration). They had a wedding dinner at Mr. Po Kim Yong's residence
2 CONC  at No. 161, Pasir Panjang Road (6 3/4 milestone) on the same day, as recorded in their wedding invitation dated 10 June 1940. The Pasir Panjang address does not correspond with the present No. 161 Pasir Panjang Road as the housin
2 CONC g numbers were renamed over the years. Po Whatt Chye fathered 11 children with Miss Cheang Lye Neo. He had 3 other wives from customary marriage and had another 8 biological children with 2 of his wives from customary marriages. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His niche is at Holy Family Church columbarium, St. Anne's section. His year of birth is recorded there incorrectly.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Updated by Nicole Evangeline Poh (grand-daughter) on 18 and 19 August 2022, with reference to the original copy of his school records, marriage certificate (two-part statutory declaration) and wedding invitation with Miss Cheang
2 CONC .
2 CONT
