1 NAME Eng Hoe /Toh/ Dato,PJK,MCH,JMN,JP,CBE,DPMP
2 GIVN Eng Hoe
2 NSFX Dato,PJK,MCH,JMN,JP,CBE,DPMP
2 _MARNM Toh
2 NICK Toh Eng Ho
1 NAME Toh Eng Hoe
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Penang
3 CTRY Malaysia
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1899
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1962
2 ADDR
3 CITY Taiping
3 STAE Perak
3 CTRY Malaysia
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/Digitised/Article/straitstimes19160822-1.2.33?ST=1&AT=search&k=Toh%20Kay%20Beng&QT=toh,kay,beng&oref=article
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1930 was a member of the perak state council.  /  Was prominent in public life.
2 CONT
2 CONT added by charles liew, grandson of eng swee.
2 CONT
2 CONT His ashes are in urn 102, next to his brothers (eng swee) urn 101, located about head level, situated under the sleeping Budha in Penang.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Taiping, Toh Eng Hoe was educated at King Edward VII School, Taiping, where he was awarded Sir William Taylor’s prize for the best essay and a silver medal as the head boy of the school in 1915. He was matriculated at Pena
2 CONC ng and went to Hong Kong University on 1916. But in a year later, he had to discontinue further studies on account of his father’s illness. With a Master of Surgery (MCh), Toh Eng Hoe was a registered doctor and served the Taiping
2 CONC  General Hospital for some years.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the death of his father, Toh Khay Beng in 1923. Toh Eng Hoe became the sole proprietor of Taik Ho & Co, well-known provision shop, Chop Guan Ho and the Taiping Spirit Distillery. He was also a well-known planter and a racehorse
2 CONC  owner and had established a motor-garage in Barrack Road (Taiping) in 1926.
2 CONT
2 CONT Being a busy man, Toh Eng Hoe had always taken an active part in public matters and was the president of the Chinese Sporting Club (Taiping), Chin Woo Athletic Association (Taiping) and the Chinese Benevolent Society. He was also 
2 CONC a senior unofficial member of the Sanitary Board of Larut & Matang, member of the Rubber Licensing Board, Small Holdings (Restriction of Sale) Committee, Public Gardens Committee, Visiting Justice to the Taiping Jail, Visitor to t
2 CONC he Larut District and General Hospitals and the Decrepit Settlement. He was also a member of the Perak State Council (1948 – 1955).
2 CONT
2 CONT Toh Eng Hoe also associated himself with all social activities and his name was a valuable asset to the Hokkien Association where he was the president and also the Taiping Literary Improvement Association, Chinese Advisory Board o
2 CONC f Perak, the Cheng Luan Seah (Penang) and a trustee of the Toh Kongsi (Penang) and a director of Taiping Cinema Ltd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Toh Eng Hoe was appointed Justice of the Peace in 1933 by the Sultan of Perak and made an Honorary Commander of the Order of the British Empire in 1956. The contributions and services of Toh Eng Hoe to the people and government of
2 CONC  Perak were credited as invaluable. He was decorated with Darjah Datuk Paduka Mahkota Perak (DPMP) which carries the title Dato. In his later life, Toh Eng Hoe was made a Member of the Order of the Defender of the Realm (AMN) for 
2 CONC his meritorious service to the country. And was conferred with a Pingat Jasa Kebaktian (PJK) by the Sultan of Perak.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://overseaschineseinthebritishempire.blogspot.com/search/label/toh%20kay%20beng
