0 @I6000000041748579872@ INDI
1 NAME Seok Neo /蔡/
2 GIVN Seok Neo
2 SURN 蔡
2 _MARNM CHUA
1 NAME CHUA Seok Neo, 蔡鍊娘
1 NAME 鍊娘 /蔡/
2 GIVN 鍊娘
2 SURN 蔡
2 _MARNM 蔡
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1837
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 APR 1927
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://mymindisrojak.blogspot.my/2014/03/mrs-wee-leong-tan-bukit-brown.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Wee Leong Tan (Bukit Brown) Madam Chua Seok Neo, one of the wife of Kapitan Cina, Wee Leong Tan of Bengkalis passed away at the age of 90 on April 12, 1927 at No. 28 Stanley Road. The tomb was cleared this year by the voluntee
2 CONC r community who call themselves "Brownies", making it accessible to visitors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Wee Leong Tan nee Madam Chua Seok Neo  Kapitan Cina of Bengkalis Wee Leong Tan alias Wee Tan (1833- April 20, 1913) came down from Amoy region at a young age and became an opium farmer under his company called chop Kim Hock Ho
2 CONC e. In his 29 years of service to the Dutch government, he was given the title Kapitan ( Capitan ) and later Major China. In 1900 he received an Imperial Order and Gold medal from Queen Wihelmina.
2 CONT
2 CONT His business expanded to shipping and also commissioning agents. He handed over his company officially to his sons to manage on 27th January 1911. His sons, Wee Kim Cheng and Wee Ann Kee made it a limited company and the shipping 
2 CONC business was acquired and incorporated in 1908 under the name of Wee Brothers Steamship Co. Ltd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wee Leong Tan was buried at the family vault in Bengkalis when he died in April 20, 1913 at the age of 78 (His wife died in 1909). He is survived by 3 sons and 3 daughters. The steamship of Wee Brothers provided free transport for
2 CONC  mourners and free loaders from Singapore to Bengkalis to attend the funeral. In the evening after the elaborate and grand burial ceremonies, the fleet provided firework displays and then set sail back to Singapore with "Will o th
2 CONC e Wisp" taking lead.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wee Ann Kee and Wee Kim Cheng, executors of their father will (source: NewspaperSG)  Wife:  name unknown Passed away in July 1909, Wee Tan's wife was shipped back to the family vault in Benkalis ( Bengkalis) for burial. There was 
2 CONC a detailed report that all ships (with exception to one) of Wee Brothers' Steamship were sent to Benkalis on the day of the funeral. The captains, officer and crew marched to the Wee family cemetery 2 miles away. Wee Tan (Wee Leon
2 CONC g Tan ) who served as the Capitan China for 35 years, expressed thanks to all present and it was estimated that no less than 8,000 people followed or witness the procession 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife: Chua Seok Neo Passed away at the age of 90 on April 12, 1927 and buried in Bukit Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs Wee Leong Tan tomb with title "Kapitan" Son: Wee Koom Poy When Wee Leong Tan retired in 1908, it was reported that his son Wee Koom Poy succeeded him. However i found no further record about him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son: Wee Kim Cheng  Wee Kim Cheng was a Senior partner of Messrs. Kim Hock Hoe and founder of Wee Brothers Steamship Co Ltd in 1908. Kim Cheng Street in Tiong Bahru area is named after him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son: Wee Ann Kee  Wee Ann Kee passed away on July 26, 1914 at his residence, No 28 Stanley Street at the age of 40. Wee Ann Kee passed away roughly a year after his father's death. He is survived by a widow and 4 sons. He was a Se
2 CONC nior Partner for Messrs. Kim Hock Hoe and of Wee Brothers Steamship Co Ltd
2 CONT
2 CONT Son: Wee Chim Yean  Mr Wee Chim Yean, Kapitan China of Benkalis passed away at the age of 41 due to pneumonia on August 12, 1926 at No 28 Stanley Road. Mr Wee Chim Yean was the youngest son of Mr Wee Leong Tan. He is survived by 4
2 CONC  sons and 4 daughters. Wee Chim Yean is buried in Bukit Brown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter: Wee Kim Lian  Wee Kim Lian married Gwee Khiok Soo.
