2 CONT Page 463, Footnote 56: Also spelt ‘Go Kek Chim’ (1896–1963). Go was the younger brother of Gaw Khek Khiam. He was educated at Raffles Institution and married Bee Twee Nio (see ‘Death’ Straits Times 7 Aug 1952, at 6). Go died on 2 
2 CONC Sep 1963, aged 67, at the General Hospital and was buried at Bidadari Christian Cemetery (see ‘Notices’ Straits Times, 14 Nov 1964, at 17; and ‘Acknowledgment’ Straits Times, 3 Sep 1963, at 11).
