1 NAME Tjeng Hiang /Thung/
2 GIVN Tjeng Hiang
2 SURN Thung
2 _MARNM Thung
1 NAME Prof.Dr.Ir. Thung Tjeng Hiang [TH10.A]
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE AUG 1897
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bogor
3 STAE West Java
3 CTRY Indonesia
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 NOV 1960
1 OCCU prof. fytopathologie
1 TITL Prof. Dr.Ir.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''''''Biography''''''
2 CONT
2 CONT Prof. Dr. Ir. T.H. Born in Bogor, West Java, on May 8, 1897 appears logical. Tjeng Hiang was adopted by Eduard C. Verschaffelt
2 CONT
2 CONT He was ELS schools in Sukabumi, then further continued at HBS, Batavia. Then continue in Agriculture Faculty Wageningen (1954) , Netherlands (Onderzoekingen over virusziekten van de boon (Phaseolus vulgaris L.)) then in Berlin, Ge
2 CONC rmany and the Institute Pasteur in Paris, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the study in the Netherlands he remained deepening of Chinese culture. Together Tjan Tjoe Som he founded the China Institute in 1930.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is an executive member CHH. After graduation, from 1926 to 1928 he worked at the Faculty of Agriculture and services for plant diseases at the University of Wageningen.
2 CONT
2 CONT After returning to the Indies, from 1929 to 1939 he worked in Proefstation voor Vortelanden Tabak (Tobacco Research Institute) for the city of Solo and Yogyakarta in Klaten, Central Java. From November 1939, he served as head of m
2 CONC ycology at the University.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1947 he was appointed as a professor at the University.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1949 he became head of the department viroli in Institure Phytopathology, Wageningen and become outstanding virology professor at the Agricultural University of Wageningen.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1949 - Prof. Dr. Ir. Thung Tjeng Hiang had meetings with parents and education experts to discuss the children's shelter is in danger of dropping out of school due the closing of a private kindergarten in Bogor. On August 22, 1949
2 CONC , established "People's School Prof. Dr. Ir. Thung" complete with facility management agency. The name of the school that used the name "Prof. Dr. Ir. Thung" was previously not approved by Prof. Thung has been elected as the first
2 CONC  Chairman of the Governing Body. The new school is opened only provide education for kindergarten only.
2 CONT
2 CONT The school is under the auspices of "Social Foundation Thung Tjoen Pok" engaged in social, educational, and teaching. Now known as Yayasan Kesatuan
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1957 he became a full professor
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1921 he had visited Tiongkok and once again done in 1960.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Fernanda Louise Willekes Macdonald at 26[1]
2 CONT He died in November 1960 at 63[2][3]
2 CONT Tjeng Hiang Thung and Fernada Louise Willekes lived in Amsterdam and had a son Paul Joan Thung, born 17 February 1924 in Amsterdam[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Tjeng Hiang Thung entered service in 1939 as a colonial civil servant and went tot he Dutch East Indies[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Sources''''''
2 CONT (Source: Leo, Prominent p. 194; Tokoh-Tokoh Etnis tionghoa di Indonesia, p. 426) (Source: Tokoh-Tokoh Etnis tionghoa di Indonesia, p. 426) (Source: E,r. Potato ./.. l'ol. 4 (1961) No. 2 (.hme)) (Source: Cyclopaedia of collectors) 
2 CONC (Source: Flora Malenesiana ser. 1.8: Cyclopaedia of collectores, Supplement II)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1↑ Marriage 1923
2 CONT 2 ↑ Death mentioned in Dutch newspaper Algemeen Handelsblad
2 CONT 3 ↑ Death 1960
2 CONT 4 ↑ Population Registration Amsterdam, Familycard Thung/Willekes
2 CONT 5 ↑ 2.10.36.21 Inventaris van het archief van het Ministerie van Koloniën: Stamkaarten Oost-Indische Ambtenaren, 1917-1952
2 CONT
2 CONT Others:
2 CONT Kepustakaan Populer Gramedia
2 CONT Etnis tionghoa di Indonesia, p. 426
2 CONT Sejarah Kesatuan
2 CONT Sekolah Kesatuan Bogor
