1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Malacca Notes. Malaya Tribune., 29 July 1916, Page 7
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral of the Late Mr Chee Sim Cheng
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral of the late Mr Chee Sim Cheng took place on Sunday the 23rd inst at 11:30a.m. After the funeral ceremony conforming to Chinese custom had been performed, the cortege, headed by a Filipino band, wended its way to Bukit 
2 CONC Sebukor where his last remains were interred in the family cemetery. One of the many wreaths sent was from the Malacca Starlight Minstrels, which Association was in the course of information by the late Mr.Chee Sim Cheng who had a
2 CONC ided them in many ways. It may be remembered that the deceased had subscribed $1500 towards the Malacca Chinese Fighter No. 2 and frequently demostrated his charitable disposition.
2 CONT
