1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chong Long Road was renamed Canning Lane. Choa Chong Long was one of the early landowners here and Earl Canning (1812--62) was a Governor-Gen-eral of India, after whom were also named a hill, a fort, a road and a r
2 CONC ise
2 CONT
2 CONT Also know as Choa Chong Lung.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secured the title to Commercial Square (now known as Raffles Place) in 1826.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died in Macao in 1838 (sources - Sinchews ruling in the Straits by Po-in Chung and The Straits Times, 12 June 1954).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://eresources.nlb.gov.sg/newspapers/digitised/article/straitstimes19540612-1.2.184.6?qt=choa,%20chong,%20long&q=Choa%20Chong%20Long
2 CONT
2 CONT Choa Chong Long was born around 1788 in Malacca and his father was a Capitan China there during Dutch control Malacca. In 1826, Choa Chong Long secured land title in Commercial Square (present Raffles Place) and built his house. H
2 CONC e was famous among the local circles and often entertained British merchants. There was a hill near Tanjong Pagar that was known as Bukit Chong Long and a road called Chong Long Road but renamed as Canning Lane (after Earl Canning
2 CONC , Governor of India, in which a road, hill and rise were name after him).In 1836, Choa Cheng Long put up an article on the newspapers that he will be leaving for China and likely be there for a few years. He never did return for C
2 CONC hoa Chong Long was murdered in Macao in 1838. 
2 CONT https://mymindisrojak.blogspot.com/2019/09/kiong-kong-tuan-kopi-sua.html
