0 @N6000000004349306715@ NOTE Died at age 26 of stroke due to high blood pressure. He was the Manager of Tiong Hua Bank (China Bank Co).
0 @N6000000004349316159@ NOTE Succeeded the father, Chan Kho in managing the family business, in
1 CONT particular Chop Chan Chin Ann.  Educated in both English and Chinese.
1 CONT Founder of Hokkien Free School in Kuching and co-sponsor of several
1 CONT temples and places of worship.  Acquired a piece of land at Matthies
1 CONT Road and constructed a mansion named 'Chin Siok Garden' which later
1 CONT became the Kuching High School administrative building.
0 @N6000000004349316167@ NOTE Affectionately referred to by grandchildren as 'Singapore grandmother'.
0 @N6000000004349058305@ NOTE Died at 1.45 pm on 6 February 1992, the 3rd day of Chinese New Year at
1 CONT his residence at 11A, Jln Ridgeway, Kuching.  Funeral Procession left
1 CONT his residence at 10.00 am on Saturday, 8 February 1992 for cremation at
1 CONT Mile 14, Old Penrissen Road, Kuching.
0 @N6000000004349360516@ NOTE Phek Khiok has 4 sons and 2 daughters.
0 @N6000000004349316290@ NOTE Became a businessman.  Settled himself in the Tabuan Road area, building
1 CONT himself a mansion on a hill surrounded by large area of land and named
1 CONT it 'Chan Chng Villa'.  Property once stretched from corner of Tabuan
1 CONT Road and Central Road East to the mansion on the mansion side and on the
1 CONT opposite side, from corner of Tabuan Road & Batu Lintang Road to just
1 CONT opposite the mansion.  Where 'Westwood Housing Estate' stands today was
1 CONT Kee Ong's "Chan's Dairy Farm" which supplied fresh milk.  Also ventured
1 CONT into Timber & Sawmilling business as well as agriculture.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was appointed as one of the 7 judges of the Chinese court when it was opened on 1 July 1912 by the Rajah.
0 @N6000000004349316185@ NOTE Affectionately referred to by grandchildren as 'Pai Teng grandmother'.
0 @N6000000004349316860@ NOTE Met with a fatal car accident while driving in the outskirts of
1 CONT Melbourne on 13 May 1974 with his wife who also succumbed to the
1 CONT accident.
0 @N6000000004349316196@ NOTE Boon Cheng (Eng Kiew’s father) was adopted by Yeo Chin, Kee Soon’s first wife when she had no children after the second wife, Bong Yeo had already given birth. After adopting Boon Cheng, Yeo Chin gave birth to Chan Kui Yaw, her on
1 CONC ly issue. Yeo Chin eventually died of breast cancer in 1945.
1 CONT
1 CONT She was affectionately referred to by grandchildren as 'Huan Cheng grandmother'.
0 @N6000000004349316213@ NOTE Together with daughter-in-law, Teo Lian Choo and grandson, Poh Tiang, she left for China in 1938. Her son, Chan Kui Seng had absconded to China just prior to that, after he went bankrupt.
1 CONT
1 CONT Eu Kek did not settle well into the new environment in ZhaoAn. Four years later in 1942, she returned to Kuching where she stayed with Chan Khiok Leng’s family at Ming Ching Road (Off Foochow Road No. 2) until her death in 1964. S
1 CONC he never returned to China again.
0 @N6000000004349316224@ NOTE Between 1933 and 1938 Chan Kui Seng absconded to China, after he went bankrupt. He had not only squandered what was bequeathed to him from Chan Chin Ann Co but also what came from the wife’s family. He took one of Chin Ann’s boat,
1 CONC  loaded with goods ordered from a whole sale company (probably the Borneo Company) on credit and left for Shantou (Swatou), where sold the goods as well as the boat. He eventually became a local ZhaoAn official of the Kuomintang G
1 CONC overnment.
1 CONT
1 CONT Kui Seng died in ZhaoAn on the 18th day of the 5th moon in 1951.
0 @N6000000004349280294@ NOTE The 3rd son of the family. Belonged to the 13th generation. Descended from the 4th son (room) of the 3rd generation. Born on the 3rd day of the 3rd moon in the year of the Pig (1839) and died on 20th day of the 7th moon in 1904 at
1 CONC  age of 66 (Chinese age). Believed to have arrived in Kuching on24th day of 12th moon 1846.  Eventually made his way to Bau to work as gardening labourer before discovering gold.  From then on whenever a person was going into the 
1 CONC gold business, he would promise the gods that should he succeed, he would give a certain percentage to Chan Kho.  In his way Chan Kho became wealthy quickly.  Later he set up Chop Chan Chin Ann.  He married the wife in China, surn
1 CONC amed Kho when his eldest son, Kee Hock was 3 years old. According to Khiok Leng, Chan Kho's forefather was from Honan and travelled down river by junk. Had 9 sons, 4 lived in Hokkien and 4 in Hakka district.
1 CONT
1 CONT Order of Chan Kho’s Sons
1 CONT 1.Chan Kee Hock – also known as ‘Tiaw Ngo’
1 CONT 2.Chan Kee Lin
1 CONT 3.Chan Kee Soon – also known as ‘Siow Liok’
1 CONT 4.Chan Kee Teck – also known as Tak San
1 CONT 5.Chan Kee Eue
1 CONT 6.Chan Kee Ong
1 CONT 7.Chan Kee Tuan
1 CONT 8.Chan  Siok Ho
1 CONT 9.Chan Kee Sian (d as a boy of 17)
1 CONT (No. 2 & No. 8 are sons of China Wife, Kho – Kee Kin was adopted)
1 CONT
1 CONT Chan Kho died in China on 20th day of the 7th moon in 1904 aged 66. When he fell ill on that trip home, a message was sent to Kuching. A belian coffin was shipped to ZhaoAn in time for his death. He was buried close to the Chan vi
1 CONC llage. In 1959, the government required the grave to be moved to make way for the Poh village and so it was exhumed and moved to the second site. The bellian coffin was found to be intact and so was not opened but reburied at the 
1 CONC new site. 
0 @N6000000004349296951@ NOTE Eldest of 3 daughters of a man believed to have come from Malacca and was doing small sundry business in the mid 1840s. Died in 1908 aged 60 at Carpenter Street, Kuching and was buried in 'Tiong Garden' at the corner of Sekama Roa
1 CONC d and Pending Road.
0 @N6000000004349306617@ NOTE Established himself in the Sekama/Pending Road area in Kuching.  One
1 CONT large property was called 'Kong Ann Garden' which was situated between
1 CONT 'Three Hills Park' and Pending Road. Died at the age of 52.
0 @N6000000004349306257@ NOTE Children are (in order of age): Boys - Kim Han, Kim Yam, Kim Cheng & (Chan) Mah Khiok; Girls - Kim Khiok & Kim Pee
0 @N6000000004349316393@ NOTE Spent most of his life in China for he was very keen to become a Chinese
1 CONT Official.  Spent a lot of money in pursuit of this objective, at least
1 CONT partially through corrupt means. He had two wives, the first of whom
1 CONT was his own first cousin, the daughter of the second sister of Chua Lian
1 CONT Married the second wife in China. He died in China in 1937 aged 72 (Chinese age).
0 @N6000000004349316409@ NOTE Spent most of his life in China. Died in his sleep.
0 @N6000000004349316443@ NOTE Died by suicide, probably due to failing financial management.
0 @N6000000004349331153@ NOTE For many years the Chief Store Keeper of Borneo Company, Kuching.
1 CONT Used to live near corner of Tabuan Road and Central Road West, where
1 CONT Central Inn is.
0 @N6000000004349331196@ NOTE Passed away at 12.10 am on Sunday, 30 July 1995.  Funeral cortege left
1 CONT 26A Jln Pisang, Kuching for funeral service at 2.00 pm on monday, 31
1 CONT July 1995 in St Faith's church, Kenyalang Park and later for burial at
1 CONT Anglican Cemetery, Batu Kitang.
0 @N6000000004349324403@ NOTE Funeral cortege left 147 Tmn Kenny at 9 am for funeral Mass at St
1 CONT Joseph's Cathedral, Kuching at 10 am on 16 October 2000 and later for
1 CONT burial at Mile 7.5 RC Cemetery
0 @N6000000004349316850@ NOTE Born in Year of Dragon.
0 @N6000000004349265006@ NOTE Born in year of cockerel.
0 @N6000000004349280722@ NOTE Resident at 48, Swee Joo Park, Kuching
0 @N6000000004349324789@ NOTE Born in Year of Monkey. Died 10 days after the birth of his 3rd child and only son, Thuan Seng.
0 @N6000000004349324810@ NOTE Born in year of Rat.
0 @N6000000004349316923@ NOTE Born on the 26th day of the 7th moon. Died with ohter membersof her immediate familyin Bau after eating wild red mushrooms. Buried in the St Stephen's Church Catholic Cemetery in Bau.
0 @N6000000004349256971@ NOTE Joseph has no sons and 1 daughter only.
0 @N6000000004349324713@ NOTE Passed away at Sarawak General Hospital on 11 January 1996.  Cortege
1 CONT left his residence 9, Kenyalang Park, Jln Berjaya for funeral service at
1 CONT 11.00 am on 13 January 1996 (Saturday) at St Faith's Church, Kenyalang
1 CONT Park, Kuching and later for burial at Anglican Cenetery, batu Kitang,
1 CONT Kuching. He was aged 70.
0 @N6000000004349316300@ NOTE Died on 12th day of the 9th Moon in the 27th Year after 1911
0 @N6000000004349256551@ NOTE Died on 6th day of 11th Moon
0 @N6000000004349306686@ NOTE Established the optical shop, Guan Ho Leong at Main Bazaar, Kuching. Geok Huat has a second wife and the optical business was given to Ong Chiang Yew, a son from his second wife.
0 @N6000000004349390901@ NOTE Died at age of 4-5 from rheumatic heart
0 @N6000000004349390912@ NOTE Died at age of 8 from typhoid
0 @N6000000004349324635@ NOTE Died at 1.30 pm on 5 February 1995 aged 69.  Funeral cortege left house
1 CONT at 4 Taman Thian Guan, Lorong Batu Lintang No 18 at 10.00 am on 7
1 CONT February for Hokkien Cemetery at Mile 8 Batu Kitang Road.  Death caused
1 CONT by cancer of digetive tract.
0 @N6000000004349265347@ NOTE Never married. Died as a bachelor.
0 @N6000000004349360950@ NOTE Died at age 19 due to train accident, possibly working for the Kuching train.
0 @N6000000004349316487@ NOTE Kee Lin was the elder son of Chan  Kho and  his China wife (surnamed ‘Kho’). Overall (among all children of Chan Kho), in order of seniority of age, Kee Lin was No. 2 after Chan Kee Hock. Kee Lin is not a natural son but was adopt
1 CONC ed through being bought from somebody.
0 @N6000000004349316517@ NOTE Siok Ho was fondly referred to as 'AngChek' (Baby Uncle). He was born when his mother, Kho was 48 years old. He was a scholar and was also referred to as 'Siew Chai'. Siok Ho is also known as Eu Chiu which was his ‘Siew Chai’ (sch
1 CONC olar) name. Siok Ho died in ZhaoAn on the 21st day of the 5th moon in 1951.
0 @N6000000004349316337@ NOTE Boon Tho was not a biological son of Kee Hock and Ang Chim but was adopted.
0 @N6000000004349324106@ NOTE Lay Eng was the only child of Chan  Kee Hock & Sim Ang Chim
0 @N6000000004349316360@ NOTE She has 3 children - 2 girls and a boy. The second girl, name unknown, was given away to a family in Dalat and was referred to by Peng Siong & siblings as "Lak Ko", meaning the 6th aunt.
0 @N6000000004349316370@ NOTE Sufferred from Leprosy and sought treatment in China where he succumbed to the disease in 1924 at the age of 37.
0 @N6000000004349296697@ NOTE He has two wives, the first of whom is Chan Lay Eng who had 4 sons.
1 CONT The second wife (name unknown) had 2 sons and 1 daughter.
0 @N6000000004349296727@ NOTE Has 4 sons & 5 daughters.
0 @N6000000004349306266@ NOTE Has 3 sons & 2 daughters
0 @N6000000004349324150@ NOTE He has only 2 daughters and no sons. It is believed that his first child was a son who died as an infant. Later Ah Chik was adopted after which Ah Chin was born.
1 CONT
1 CONT Mah Khiok used go sting badminton rackets.
0 @N6000000004349346202@ NOTE Died aged 40 in 1935, believed to be poisoned by his secretary who was charged with the responsibility of looking after his properties. The intention of the murder was to take over his properties. Kim Han was apparently having a g
1 CONC ambling session and drinking coffee which may contain the poison. He died the next day and his extremities turned black.
0 @N6000000004349346213@ NOTE After marriage, husband took her to China where she lived for many years but later returned to Kuching. She died in Kuching.
0 @N6000000004349311207@ NOTE Born on the 8th day of the 10th moon in 1885
0 @N6000000004349316433@ NOTE Died on the 25th day of the 9th moon in 1958
0 @N6000000004349324053@ NOTE 3rd son of Chan Kee Teck but was 'adopted' by Chan Kee Sian who died as a bachelor at age 17. Key Cho & his wife Ho Bee Hian has only one daughter, Boi Hong and no sons. Keng Liat, biological son of Kwang Cho, Key Cho's older biol
1 CONC ogical brother, was adopted as a son
0 @N6000000004349244833@ NOTE Died at 9.25 pm on 19 December 1992.  Funeral procession left 127B, KMC
1 CONT Flats, Jln Ban Hock on Monday 21 December 1992 at 10.00 am for Hokkien
